WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.682
"Help!" Gliss shrieked. The wind had knocked her down and was whipping her hair over her face.

2
00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:10.414
She was now struggling to hang onto the edge of the chasm.

3
00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:16.431
"Hold on!" Darb lunged toward her, but he ended up almost falling over the edge himself.

4
00:00:16.432 --> 00:00:24.611
Zing flew overhead, whistling with alarm. A gust of wind grabbed the dragon, tossing him end over end.

5
00:00:24.612 --> 00:00:27.532
"To me!" Wyssa shouted.

6
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:31.893
Suddenly Zann felt himself being grabbed by magical energy.

7
00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:35.992
It yanked him backward, away from the terrifying drop-off.

8
00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:40.143
Soon the entire group was safely out of the wind's reach.

9
00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:44.039
"Wow, that was close!" Perda exclaimed.

10
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:50.324
Venna nodded. "No wonder Prince Doni warned us that the Gray Gorge was very dangerous."

11
00:00:50.325 --> 00:00:55.433
Darb stared up at the stone tower. "That looks like Morb's kind of place."

12
00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:59.330
"Yeah," Zann agreed. "And my parents are in there!"

13
00:00:59.331 --> 00:01:02.889
His heart pounded at the thought that they might be so close.

14
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:07.244
After all this time, was he finally going to be with them again?

15
00:01:07.245 --> 00:01:11.396
"How are we going to get in there?" Gliss wondered.

16
00:01:11.397 --> 00:01:21.272
"Good question," Zann muttered. The tower was perched halfway across a narrow, ancient-looking stone bridge spanning the Gray Gorge.

17
00:01:21.273 --> 00:01:25.439
"Prince Doni said Morb built this place," Perda said.

18
00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:31.567
"It must have taken a lot of magic to do that, especially in a spot like this."

19
00:01:31.568 --> 00:01:42.774
"Indeed." Wyssa sounded grim. "It seems he must have figured out a new way to steal magic. Lots of magic." Zann

20
00:01:42.775 --> 00:01:50.188
studied the tower. "The wind will make it hard to cross the bridge without falling into the gorge," he said. "But

21
00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:53.138
otherwise, it doesn't look that bad. The

22
00:01:53.139 --> 00:01:55.736
gate is small enough to step over." He

23
00:01:55.737 --> 00:01:59.768
pointed to a short gate blocking the entrance to the bridge. "I

24
00:01:59.769 --> 00:02:03.978
suppose it's only meant to keep Roodians out," Venna said. "Yeah.

25
00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:08.031
Or keep them in ," Gliss added.

26
00:02:08.032 --> 00:02:11.795
"I doubt they're thrilled to be Morb's servants."

27
00:02:11.796 --> 00:02:15.796
"So what are we waiting for?" Perda took a step toward the bridge.

28
00:02:15.797 --> 00:02:21.602
Wyssa narrowed her eyes. "It seems odd that there's no sentry."

29
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:28.006
"Yes, it does," Venna said. "I'm sure Morb must have some sort of Shield spell on the place."

30
00:02:28.007 --> 00:02:31.215
"There's only one way to find out. Come on!"

31
00:02:31.216 --> 00:02:40.649
Zann hurried toward the bridge. Bracing himself against the gusty wind, he stepped over the gate. Perda was right behind him.

32
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:47.269
"Wait," Wyssa called from the other side of the gate. She pointed past Zann. "What's that?"

33
00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:55.212
Zann peered through the fog. Something was sitting on the bridge just ahead. It was small and fluffy.

34
00:02:55.213 --> 00:02:59.186
"Oh!" Zann exclaimed. "It must be the missing mibbit!"

35
00:02:59.187 --> 00:03:03.319
"Aw, it's cute." Perda smiled and stepped forward.

36
00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.577
"Wait," Zann said. "It looks kind of tense."

37
00:03:07.578 --> 00:03:14.698
"Here, mibbit, mibbit!" Perda cooed. She grabbed for the creature. It squawked and leaped back.

38
00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:23.616
"Careful, don't panic it or—" Zann gasped as a shock wave of magic energy hit him. He saw Perda collapse to her knees.

39
00:03:23.617 --> 00:03:28.982
The mibbit was sending out confusing energy waves, just like Vee had described!

40
00:03:28.983 --> 00:03:32.234
Zann had never felt anything like it before.

41
00:03:32.235 --> 00:03:38.347
He couldn't move or think clearly. Unlike with the scatter beast attack, though, there was no pain.

42
00:03:38.348 --> 00:03:45.505
Still, he felt completely helpless. What if Morb looked out a window and spotted him and Perda on the bridge?

43
00:03:45.506 --> 00:03:52.107
He heard moans from behind him. With great effort he turned his head far enough to see the others.

44
00:03:52.108 --> 00:03:55.731
Venna was clinging to a tree, gasping for breath.

45
00:03:55.732 --> 00:04:03.459
Gliss was on the ground, helpless—and sliding toward the dizzying drop-off! Zing wasn't far behind her.

46
00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.979
Zann wanted to save them. But he still couldn't move.

47
00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.005
In fact, he realized he and Perda were dangerously close to the edge too.

48
00:04:12.006 --> 00:04:14.942
He looked for Wyssa, hoping she could help them.

49
00:04:14.943 --> 00:04:18.150
But she looked just as helpless as the others.

50
00:04:18.151 --> 00:04:22.078
She'd stopped herself from rolling over the edge by clutching the gate.

51
00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:25.117
But Zann could see that her grip was weakening.

52
00:04:25.118 --> 00:04:27.804
Another wave of magic struck them all.

53
00:04:27.805 --> 00:04:30.899
Zann felt himself teetering on the edge of the bridge.

54
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.035
Was this the end for him—for all of them?

55
00:04:34.036 --> 00:04:36.645
Then he saw movement near the gate.

56
00:04:36.646 --> 00:04:41.906
He couldn't turn his head, but he rolled his eyes far enough to see what was happening.

57
00:04:41.907 --> 00:04:45.562
It was Darb! He was jumping over the small gate.

58
00:04:45.563 --> 00:04:49.283
Dodging Zann and Perda, Darb hurried over to the mibbit. "Easy,

59
00:04:49.284 --> 00:04:53.021
little fellow," Darb said soothingly. He

60
00:04:53.022 --> 00:04:58.702
gently picked up the mibbit and stroked its ears, just as Vee had taught them. A

61
00:04:58.703 --> 00:05:02.395
moment later the energy waves were gone. "Whoa!"

62
00:05:02.396 --> 00:05:07.639
Perda gasped, sitting up and moving herself away from the drop—off. Zann

63
00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:11.285
did the same. "Thanks, Darb," he said. "But

64
00:05:11.286 --> 00:05:14.635
why didn't the mibbit's magic affect you?" Darb

65
00:05:14.636 --> 00:05:20.428
shrugged, cuddling the mibbit. The fluffy creature looked happy and relaxed now. "Maybe

66
00:05:20.429 --> 00:05:23.050
it's because I'm a Void," he said. "I

67
00:05:23.051 --> 00:05:25.845
don't have any magic for the mibbit to affect." Wyssa

68
00:05:25.846 --> 00:05:29.816
nodded. "I think you must be right, boy." Zing

69
00:05:29.817 --> 00:05:35.615
flew toward Darb. He circled him, sniffing at the mibbit curiously. "Down,

70
00:05:35.616 --> 00:05:41.159
boy," Zann told his dragon. "That mibbit is not a snack!" Venna

71
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:45.318
brushed the dirt off her clothes and frowned at the mibbit. "I'm

72
00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:51.509
guessing that thing was supposed to be Morb's security guard," she said. "Shall we proceed?" Zann

73
00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.012
opened his mouth to say yes. But

74
00:05:54.013 --> 00:05:59.886
his words were lost as an eerie howl echoed from the depths of the gorge. Gliss'

75
00:05:59.887 --> 00:06:04.166
eyes widened. "What was that ?"

76
00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:12.392
Before anyone could respond, a huge head on a long, snakelike neck arose from the dark gorge.

77
00:06:12.393 --> 00:06:17.522
The orange glow of its eyes cut through the fog like flames.

78
00:06:17.523 --> 00:06:22.779
With a loud roar, the creature exposed a mouth full of sharp fangs.

79
00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:32.654
Wyssa went pale. "It's the Beast of the Otherworld!"

